-- title:
--   Convergence of twisted orbital integrals at a regular diagonal class
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields, let $\nu_{Z}$ be a Haar measure on the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ (with its Borel structure) and let $\Omega_L$ be a fundamental domain for the image of $L^\times$ in $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ with respect to $\nu_Z$. Let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$, i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the continuous ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ compatible with the embedding of $L$, let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and write $\sigma_D$ for the induced automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$. Let $\xi$ be a homomorphism from the full subgroup of $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ whose associated function $z \mapsto \xi(z)$ is continuous and trivial on the image of $L^\times$; no $\sigma$-invariance of $\xi$ is assumed. Let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ have vanishing off-diagonal entries and satisfy $N_{L/K}(\delta_{0,00}/\delta_{0,11}) \neq 1$. Let $I \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be the set of $\delta$ for which some $g$ makes $\delta_0^{-1}(g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(g))$ central, let $\Lambda$ be the subgroup of those $\gamma$ with $\delta_0^{-1}(\gamma\delta_0\,\sigma(\gamma)^{-1})$ central, and let $r : \iota \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, $\iota$ countable, be such that each $\gamma$ satisfies $(r\,i)^{-1}\gamma \in \Lambda$ for exactly one $i$. Let $H$ be the closed subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ consisting exactly of the matrices $h$ with vanishing off-diagonal entries such that $\sigma_D(h)h^{-1}$ is central, with $\mu_H$ a right-invariant Haar measure, and equip the orbit quotient $H \backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ with the measure obtained by pushing forward the adelic Haar measure `adelicGLHaar`, weighted by the density of the module `HaarQuotient`. Let $\varphi$ be continuous with compact support on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, and set $$F^{\sharp}(y) = \int^{-}\!\!\|\xi(z)\|\,\bigl\|\varphi\bigl(y^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma_D(z\cdot y)\bigr)\bigr\|\,d\nu_Z(z),\qquad F(y) = \int \xi(z)\,\varphi\bigl(y^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma_D(z\cdot y)\bigr)\,d\nu_Z(z),$$ where $\delta_0$ is viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ through the entrywise embedding of $L$ and $z$ acts as the central scalar matrix. Then, with $q \mapsto q^{\mathrm{out}}$ the canonical section of the quotient, $w$ the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ of the antidiagonal matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathcal{H}$ the adelic height: (i) there is a compact $C \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ such that $F^{\sharp}(y) \neq 0$ implies $y \in H \cdot C$; (ii) $\int^{-} F^{\sharp}(q^{\mathrm{out}})\,dq < \infty$; (iii) $q \mapsto \|F(q^{\mathrm{out}})\|$ is integrable; (iv) the integral of $\bigl|-\log \mathcal{H}(q^{\mathrm{out}}) - \log \mathcal{H}(w\,q^{\mathrm{out}})\bigr| \cdot F^{\sharp}(q^{\mathrm{out}})$ is finite; (v) the same height weight times $\|F(q^{\mathrm{out}})\|$ is integrable; and (vi) there is $M \in \mathbb{R}$ with $\mathcal{H}(q^{\mathrm{out}})\,\mathcal{H}(w\,q^{\mathrm{out}}) \le M$ whenever $F^{\sharp}(q^{\mathrm{out}}) \neq 0$.
--
--   This is the absolute-convergence statement for the $\sigma$-twisted orbital integral, and for its height-weighted variant, attached to a diagonal class $\delta_0$ whose ratio of diagonal entries has norm different from $1$; the character $\xi$ is not assumed $\sigma$-invariant, so only the absolute values of the twisted orbital integrals are controlled. It supports the geometric side of the twisted trace formula comparison and is used by [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_tsum_norm_bracket_mul_twistedOrbital_lt_top_and_integrableOn`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_tsum_norm_bracket_mul_twistedOrbital_lt_top_and_integrableOn).
